.SH "Detailed Description"
.PP 
Provides FP8‑format specific parameters required for MX‑block arithmetic\&. 

Implementations expose the structural properties of an FP8 type such as: 
.PD 0
.IP "\(bu" 2
The mantissa bit mask 
.IP "\(bu" 2
The maximum exponent value 
.IP "\(bu" 2
The shift‑raster used for MX mantissa alignment 
.PP
These values allow \fRFloat8UMX{T}\fP to operate generically across different FP8 formats (e\&.g\&., E5M2, E4M3, E3M4) without hard‑coded constants\&. 

.PP
\fBTemplate Parameters\fP
.RS 4
\fITbase\fP The underlying numeric type used to represent FP8 bit‑fields (typically \fR\fBFast_Byte\fP\fP or \fRbyte\fP)\&. 
.RE
.PP

